  "body": "Found in review of PR #1535 (#1526), by M5.\n\n**What happens.** After #1535, a post-option edit on a setup page in a document with two or more setups becomes that setup's own options. So the setups can now differ in their options with one click.\n\nA whole-program post already refuses by name when setups differ in **Output** or **Threading** (`program_problems`). It does not check **End units**: it takes End units from the active setup. A program with Setup1 set to \"end in inch\" and Setup2 to \"end in mm\" posts whichever the active setup says, and does not say so.\n\n**Expected.** Either the whole-program post refuses by name when setups differ in End units, as it does for Output and Threading, or the End-units word is taken from one documented rule and said in the output header. Never silently from whichever setup happens to be active.\n\n**Workaround.** Post the setups one at a time, or keep End units the same on every setup.\n\n**Done means.** A two-setup document with different End units either refuses the whole-program post by name, or posts the documented rule's word. This is pinned, with a mutation check.\n\nRelated: #1526, #1527, #1535.\n",
